---
import BlogArticleShell from '../../../components/BlogArticleShell.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const canonicalPath = '/blog/kakobuy-jersey-sportswear-spreadsheet-lane-2026';
const publishedISO = '2026-06-14';
---

<BlogArticleShell
  title="Jersey & sportswear on the Kakobuy Spreadsheet: 2026 lane guide | kakobuy-cn.com"
  description="A data-backed guide to jersey rows on kakobuy-cn.com—22 catalogue cards, Nike/Jordan/Adidas clusters, patch QC, and sizing for football and basketball kits."
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  headline="Jersey lane guide: football and basketball kits on the Kakobuy Spreadsheet (2026)"
  publishedISO={publishedISO}
  displayDate="14 June 2026"
  structuredKeywords={[
    'Kakobuy Spreadsheet jersey',
    'football kit reps guide 2026',
    'Nike Jordan jersey QC',
    'Mitchell Ness spreadsheet',
    'kakobuy-cn.com jersey lane',
  ]}
>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    Jersey season spikes twice a year—club transfers and World Cup cycles—and spreadsheet rows multiply with badge-heavy kits that fail QC on number spacing alone.
    Our <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> <a href="/category/jersey/">Jersey</a> lane indexes <strong>22 rows</strong> as of <strong>14 June 2026</strong>, led by <strong>Nike</strong>, <strong>Jordan</strong>, <strong>Adidas</strong>, and <strong>Mitchell &amp; Ness</strong> (three rows each in the snapshot).
  </p>

  <h2>June 2026 jersey snapshot</h2>
  <div class="blog-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Label</th><th scope="col">Rows</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Adidas, Jordan, Mitchell &amp; Ness, Nike, Other</td><td>3 each</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Errea, Joma</td><td>2 each</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Total</td><td>22</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Kit types in the feed</h2>
  <h3>Current-season club (Nike, Adidas)</h3>
  <p>
    Sponsor logo alignment and sleeve patch placement are non-negotiable QC points.
    Sellers rotate seasons quickly—verify year in listing title matches photos.
  </p>
  <h3>Retro &amp; throwback (Mitchell &amp; Ness)</h3>
  <p>
    Heavier mesh and different sizing curves; compare shoulder width flat-lay to chart.
  </p>
  <h3>Basketball (Jordan)</h3>
  <p>
    Swingman vs authentic-tier chatter applies—price band hints at material but warehouse photos decide.
  </p>

  <h2>QC checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Number and name letter spacing; heat-press vs stitch</li>
    <li>Club crest colour layers and star count</li>
    <li>Collar tag fonts and size label</li>
    <li>Length vs size—kits run long</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Pair with <a href="/blog/kakobuy-sizing-spreadsheet-apparel/">sizing guide</a> and <a href="/blog/kakobuy-sneakers-spreadsheet-lane-guide-2026/">sneakers lane</a> for full fit pics.
  </p>

  <h2>Shipping</h2>
  <p>
    Jerseys are lightweight freight allies in mixed hauls.
    Branded team kits may still flag trademark routing—<a href="/blog/shipping-branded-vs-unbranded-spreadsheet-restrictions/">branded lines</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Workflow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet home</a></strong> → <a href="/category/jersey/">Jersey</a>.</li>
    <li>Confirm player/name variant before paste.</li>
    <li>QC patches and numbers; reject misaligned transfers.</li>
  </ol>
</BlogArticleShell>
